2. Do you receive any 1099-NEC or 1099-MISC from the two clients? (You must report all self-employment income even if you didn’t get a 1099.)  
3. Do you pay your utilities or internet separately (and do you want to include a portion of these for the home-office actual-expense method)?  
4. Any mortgage interest, property taxes, or big medical expenses that you haven’t listed? (Could affect itemizing decision.)

Other practical advice
- Keep receipts for the $1,400 charitable gift (you said you have the receipt) and for all business expenses and student loan interest statements (Form 1098-E or statements from MOHELA).  
- If you expect similar self-employment income in the coming year, consider quarterly estimated tax payments to avoid penalties.  
