  b) Actual method: Deduct the business percentage of actual home expenses (rent, utilities, renter’s insurance, etc.). Your business percentage = 155 / 780 = 0.1987 ≈ 19.9%. Annual rent = $2,100 × 12 = $25,200; business-share of rent ≈ $5,011 (0.1987 × $25,200). Add business-share of utilities, internet (portion used for business), etc. The actual method usually gives a larger deduction here because your rent is relatively high.
