- The student loan interest deduction is an adjustment to income (an “above-the-line” deduction) with a maximum of $2,500 in most years and AGI phaseouts. It is based on interest you paid in the tax year (you should receive Form 1098‑E from MOHELA showing interest paid). You cannot deduct the full $4,800 if the $4,800 is interest paid in one year — the max is $2,500 (unless rules change). With your combined income (~$95k gross before adjustments), you are likely not in the phaseout range and should be able to take the allowed $2,500 (confirm with your final AGI).

