- If these are unreimbursed employee expenses (for a W-2 job), they are not deductible on the federal return for tax years through 2025 (suspended by TCJA).
- If they are business expenses related to your graphic design self-employment, include them on Schedule C (they reduce your net self-employment income).

Self‑employment tax and related adjustments
- You’ll owe self‑employment tax (Social Security + Medicare) on your net self‑employment earnings — calculated on Schedule SE. The self‑employment tax is roughly 15.3% on net earnings (net of the 7.65% employer share adjustment), and half of that SE tax is an above‑the‑line deduction on Schedule 1 (reduces AGI).
- The home office deduction and other Schedule C expenses reduce your net self‑employment income and therefore reduce both income tax and self‑employment tax.

