2. Decide home‑office computation: quick compare simplified ($775) vs regular (≈19.9% of eligible home expenses). If you want, give me the annual utility/internet/insurance amounts and I can estimate both methods and show which gives a bigger deduction.
3. Run the math or use tax software / CPA: include W-2 wages, interest, net Schedule C profit (after home office and business expenses), the student loan interest adjustment (max $2,500 subject to MAGI), and then decide standard vs itemize. I can help do the computation if you want me to estimate taxable income and tax liability using the numbers you gave.
