2) Student loan interest ($4,800 listed) — important clarification needed
- The student loan interest deduction is an above-the-line adjustment (up to $2,500 in most cases) for interest you actually paid in the tax year. You can’t claim interest paid in prior years on this year’s return. Also there are MAGI phaseouts for the deduction (the deduction phases out for higher incomes for MFJ).
